 "mcmc_conv_txt": "The chains were continued from their last state until a maximum $\\hat R$ below 1.1 and retained draws (the second half of each chain) spanning at least 50 integrated autocorrelation times, or until the available computing time was exhausted. Neither chain met these criteria: after {{c2_mcmc_iter}} iterations for C2 and {{c1_mcmc_iter}} for C1, $\\hat R$ was up to {{c2_max_rhat}} and {{c1_max_rhat}}, and the retained draws spanned only {{c2_n_iat}} and {{c1_n_iat}} times the longest autocorrelation times ({{c2_max_iat_post}} and {{c1_max_iat_post}} iterations). The slowest directions involved the radiative partition and the transfer coefficients (Figure S2). All posterior intervals (Table [tab:priors] and the scenario band) are therefore indicative, whereas the posterior modes, on which the mechanism, map and Sobol analyses rest, are not affected.",
 "mcmc_disc_txt": "the ensemble sampler mixed slowly, above all along the ridge between the skin and near-surface absorption bands and in the transfer coefficients (integrated autocorrelation times of up to {{c2_max_iat_post}} iterations; Figure S2), and the chains had not met the convergence criteria, so all posterior intervals are indicative; ",
